      "position_evidence": "inferred",
      "position_frame": null,
      "provenance": "literature_retrieved",
      "rationale": "[Literature audit 2026-11-05 (deliverome-analysis PR 236), verdict region_only: insert_after_residue 594 -> NULL; the paper names a region, not a junction (region: nucleotide 1782 after the start codon (codon 594 or 595)). Paper (PMID 24386311): \"A Flag tag was inserted into CLCA4 sequence at nucleotide position1782 after the start codon.\". Audit note: Secondary sources checked: PMC3873418 full text has no primer sequences, and the Europe PMC supplement is only pone.0083943.s001.tif (a figure) plus figure/table images; no supplementary methods or plasmid deposit. Species of the Open Biosystems cDNA still unstated. The 594|595 (row) vs 595|596 ambiguity cannot be resolved from the paper.] Nucleotide 1782 after the start codon falls exactly at the end of codon 594 (codon 594 occupies nt 1780\u20131782; computed as 1782/3 = 594.0), placing the FLAG insertion after residue 594 (I) and before residue 595 (T). Residue 594 lies within the extracellular span 22\u2013919 confirmed by topology landmarks. The tag is validated at this exact nucleotide-defined junction by Western blot expression and a functional colony-formation assay showing preserved tumour-suppressor activity, though explicit surface-detection of the FLAG epitope was not reported. Ranked second because surface localisation was not directly demonstrated. Full-length CLCA4 with a FLAG tag inserted at nucleotide position 1782 after the start codon, lentivirally transduced into MCF7 breast cancer cells. Expression confirmed by Western blot (L5). Colony formation assay used to assess proliferation inhibition.",
